A(('p', '**Step 3. Compare with the neighbors.** Read Luke 14:16–24 and write down what is in Luke’s story that is not in Matthew’s, and what is in Matthew’s that is not in Luke’s. Read Matthew 21:33–41 and write who is sent and what happens to them. Write whether Jesus connects either passage to Matthew 22.'))
A(('p', '**Step 4. Mark stated and not stated.** Using two colors, mark each statement in Section 5 of this study as “stated by the story” or “arising from the comparison.” If a statement is neither, strike it out.'))
A(('p', '**Step 5. Write the boundary.** In two sentences, write where Jesus told this parable and what He was preaching, using Matthew 21:23, 4:17 and 10:5–7.'))

